\begin{abstract}
A CR-dynamical system is a pair $\p{X, G}$, where $X$ is a non-empty compact Hausdorff space with uniformity $\collection{U}$ and $G$ is a closed relation on $X$. In this paper we introduce the $\p{i, j}$-shadowing properties in CR-dynamical systems, which generalises the shadowing property from topological dynamical systems $\p{X, f}$. This extends previous work on shadowing in set-valued dynamical systems. 
\end{abstract}

