is a $\delta$-pseudo-orbit in  $\p{X_G^+, \sigma_G^+}$. However, it is not $\epsilon$-shadowed by any point in $X_G^+$: to derive a contradiction, suppose $\sequenceOf{y_N}:{N \in \omega}$ $\epsilon$-shadows our $\delta$-pseudo-orbit. Then, 
\[
\sum_{k = 0}^\infinity \Fraction d\of{0, y_k} / {2^{k+1}} < \Fraction 1 / {54},
