implying $d\of{0, y_0} < \Fraction 1 / {27}$. Therefore, $y_N \subseteq [0, \Fraction 2 / 9] \intersect X$ for each $N \in \omega$. Since $\lim_{k\to +\infinity} b_k = \Fraction 1 / 3$, there exists $\ell \geq m$, such that $d\of{\Fraction 1 / 3, b_\ell} < \Fraction 1 / {27}$. We must have $d\of{b_\ell, y_{n + \ell - m + 1}} < \Fraction 1 / {27}$, since
