\subsection{Fractional Boundary Value Problem (FrBVP)}\label{P4_BVP}
%Let us consider the system of fractional differential equation \eqref{P4_problem} with $k_1=5, \gamma_1 = 1, f_1(\x, \y,\z)= - 8 \exp{(\y-1)} + 2 \exp{\Big(-(\frac{\z-1}{2})\Big)}$ and $k_2= 3, \gamma_2= 1, f_2(\x, \y, \z)= 8 \exp{(-(\z-1))} +\exp{\Big(\frac{\y-1}{2}\Big)},$ subject to boundary conditions $\y'(0)=0, \y(1)=1-2\log{2}, \z'(0) =0, \z(1) = 1+2 \log{2}.$
