In region \circled{1}, there are two natural normalizations we can use 
\begin{equation}\label{defPsi1su2}
\Psi_{\rm red}^{\text{norm}_1,(1)}=\e^{\frac{\Upsilon_{\rm red}^{\text{norm}_1,(1)}(z,\epsilon)}{\epsilon}},
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}\label{defPsi2su2}
\Psi_{\rm red}^{\text{norm}_2,(1)}=\e^{\frac{\Upsilon_{\rm red}^{\text{norm}_2,(1)}(z,\epsilon)}{\epsilon}},
\end{equation}
depending on which branch point and which soliton we use in \eqref{Upsilonallorder}. To be more precise, norm$_{1,2}$ correspond to using $b_0=\pm \ri$ and $-\gamma_{21_{1,2}}$ for regularization respectively.
