\textbf{\emph{Effect of noise.}}--- We now discuss the effect of noise on the expectation value $\Tr[\rho_{\rm ave} (X\otimes \mathcal{O})]$. We use $\langle X\otimes \mathcal{O} \rangle$ to denote the noisy expectation values, while $\Tr[\rho_{\rm ave} (X\otimes O)]$ denotes the noiseless expectation value.


% Errors on the ancilla of $\rho_{\rm ave}$ are relatively rare because only a proportion $O(1/N)$ of the total gates act on the ancilla. Their effect is also particularly simple to describe. $Z$ errors multiply by $-1$ the two terms in \eqref{rho} where $e^{\pm iHt}$ appears. Denoting $p_Z$ the $Z$ error rate per unit time on the ancilla, we have thus
