  Let \((X, d, \mu)\) be a space of homogeneous type and \(\d\) a dyadic system with parameters \(c_0, C_0\), and \(\delta\). Suppose that \(\operatorname{diam}(X) = \infty\), take \(\dada \geq \frac{3 A_0^2}{\delta}\), and set \(E \subseteq X\) satisfy \(0 < \operatorname{diam}(E) < \infty\). Then there exists a partition \(\mathcal{D}' \subseteq \d\) of \(X\) such that \(E \subseteq \dada P\) for all \(Q \in \mathcal{D}'\).
