where we used the disjointness of $\{E_B\}_{B \in \S}$ and that $B \subseteq B^3_0$ for all $B \in \S$. 
Note that the implicit constants above do not depend on $\S$. Consequently, combining \eqref{Tf-sparse}, \eqref{BBSS}, and \eqref{eq:ASB} yields \eqref{TbM-2}.

Now only the proofs for \eqref{Tf-sparse} and \eqref{BBSS} remain. From $\bigcup\limits_{i=1}^m\supp(f_i) \subseteq B_0$ and the proof of Theorem \ref{S.d.main}, it derives that \eqref{Tf-sparse}.
To prove \eqref{BBSS}, we observe that 
