\begin{definition}
We say that $A_{\infty, \B}$ satisfies the {\bf sharp reverse H\"{o}lder property} if there exists a constant $c_0>0$ such that for every $w \in A_{\infty, \B}$ one has $w \in RH_{r_w, \B}$ with $r_w = 1 + c_0 [w]_{A_{\infty, \B}}^{-1}$.  
\end{definition}
