   \caption{(a) Illustration of the approach to the thermodynamic limit by expanding the size of a fractal pattern. At each step, the total linear size $L$ is multiplied by three, while the smallest resolved feature $l$ remains constant. (b–d): Minimal asymptotic decay rate $\lambda_{\min}$ as a function of the linear system size $L$ for detuning values $\Delta = 1.0\gamma$, $\Delta = 2.0\gamma$, and $\Delta = 3.0\gamma$. Different markers correspond to different spatial geometries indicated in the legend.
    }
