meaning $H_\theta (e) (x)^{(2)} = c(x)^{(2)}$. Now $e(x)^{(2)}$ is inductively defined for all $x < 0$. Assume then that $e(x+2)^{(1)}, e(x+3)^{(1)}, \ldots, e(x+n+1)^{(1)}$ have been defined. If $\theta(x) = \delta_n$ and $\theta (x+1) = \delta_n$, let
