    A_k$. The orange region illustrates the second case, in which $\dist(U(x),\K) \geq C$. The smaller circles denote the projections $A_{k-1} \cdot \zeta, A_k \cdot \zeta, A_{k+1} \cdot \zeta$. The thin lines are the
    boundaries of the Voronoi-regions. }
