Function Calling implementations collapse LLM orchestration, tool registry, and execution into tightly coupled API endpoints, relying heavily on JSON formatting in both tool schema definitions and agent-tool interactions. This design introduces broad injection and manipulation threat surfaces, with successful API parameter interception or JSON injection potentially compromising both reasoning and actuation layers simultaneously. As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:asr_comparison}, Function Calling achieves an overall ASR of 73.5\% compared to MCP's 62.59\%.

