Let $u=\< X,\nu \> $ be the support function of $X$, and $\hat{u}:=G(\nu_F)(\nu_F,X)$ be the anisotropic support function of $X$ with respect to $F$(or $\W$). Then we have (see e.g. \cite{Xia2017})
\begin{equation}
	\label{u-hatu}
	\hat{u}=\frac{u}{F(\nu)}.
\end{equation}
