			%let $\Gamma$ denote the 2-dimensional plane spanned by  vectors $E_{n+1}$ and $\nu(\xi)$ (if $E_{n+1}=\nu(\xi)$, let $\Gamma$ be any arbitrarily chosen 2-dimensional plane passing through $E_{n+1}$). The plane $\Gamma$ intersects  $\mathcal{C}_{\omega_0}$ along a curve, of which we parametrize a segment as $\gamma:[0,1]\to \mathcal{C}_{\omega_0}$, which satisfies $\gamma(0)=\xi,\gamma(1)=\xi_0\in\partial\mathcal{C}_{\omega_0}$.
